+// am3_mojo fix: the index of the grid point at or below the position x on a
+// grid (in units of its spacing). Below the start of the grid, it is the
+// index of the point above. The index is x truncated, but a position within
+// 1e-9 of a whole number is that number. (For 2 to 4 % of the points, the
+// logarithm of a point's own energy, divided by the spacing, comes out
+// slightly below its index. The truncation alone took these points to the
+// point below.)
+static int grid_index(double x){
+	double r = floor(x + 0.5);
+	if (fabs(x - r) < 1e-9) return (int)r;
+	return (int)x;}
